# GeckOS with a disk in the drive that has its programs: the shell on the
# console comes from there, c:, and the card is not read at all. With -r the
# bytes of the drive come at their baud rate, wanted or not: none is lost.
# rom: geckos
# disk: geckos
# emu: -r
# expect: geckos: hello, it is 20
# expect: Start "fsflop": ok!
# expect: Start "c:lsh -d c:": ok!
# expect: lsh read, 7393 bytes
# expect: |FLOPPY
# expect: |lsmem
# expect: Bytes free.
# expect: SD reads=0
# expect: overruns=0
wait 14
screen
kbd ls\r
wait 6
screen
quit
